Rule O1 (doc/scope_model.mld, sections 3.1 and 7) for a root that is stored
in the file of a unit other than its origin. The origin of a root is the
unit whose source it came from. A root with no digest is looked up among
the libraries its origin was compiled with, Λc(o) (rule P2, section 3.2).
Λc(u) is the set of libraries given with [-L] when the unit [u] was
compiled (section 1).

The library [lib] is built as dune builds a wrapped library with the
member [Bar]. dune generates the alias module [lib.ml-gen], compiled as
the unit [Lib], with [module Bar = Lib__Bar] and a [@canonical] tag. It
compiles it first, with [-nopervasives -nostdlib -w -49]. Then it
compiles [bar.mli] as the hidden unit [Lib__Bar], with [-open Lib]. [Lib]
records no digest for [Lib__Bar], as it is a pure alias. [libv] is a
vendored copy of [lib], built from the same sources. The library [c] is
built against [lib]; [c.mli] is [include module type of Lib]. No unit sees
both [lib] and [libv] (D3, section 2). Every compile uses dune's
[-no-alias-deps], and [-L] for the unit's own library and its
dependencies.

  $ cat lib/lib.ml-gen
  (* generated by dune *)
  
  (** @canonical Lib.Bar *)
  module Bar = Lib__Bar
  $ cat libv/lib.ml-gen
  (* generated by dune *)
  
  (** @canonical Lib.Bar *)
  module Bar = Lib__Bar
  $ cat lib/bar.mli
  type t
  $ cat libv/bar.mli
  type t
  $ cat c/c.mli
  include module type of Lib
  $ for l in lib libv; do
  >   ocamlc -bin-annot -no-alias-deps -nopervasives -nostdlib -w -49 -I $l -o $l/lib.cmo -c -impl $l/lib.ml-gen
  >   ocamlc -bin-annot -no-alias-deps -I $l -open Lib -o $l/lib__Bar.cmi -c -intf $l/bar.mli
  > done
  $ ocamlc -bin-annot -no-alias-deps -I lib -c c/c.mli

odoc compiles the units in the order dune built them. When [Lib] is
compiled, [Lib__Bar] is not compiled yet, so the root [Lib__Bar] is left
for link (section 7).

  $ for l in lib libv; do
  >   odoc compile --output-dir h --parent-id pkg/$l -L $l:h/pkg/$l $l/lib.cmt
  >   odoc compile --output-dir h --parent-id pkg/$l -L $l:h/pkg/$l $l/lib__Bar.cmti
  > done
  $ odoc compile --output-dir h --parent-id pkg/c -L c:h/pkg/c -L lib:h/pkg/lib c/c.cmti

How to read [odoc_print --short --long-paths --show-root-parents]. Each line
is one item of the signature. [Bar/0] is the item [Bar], with a number odoc
adds to tell apart items of the same name. [resolved(...)] is a resolved
path, and [root(pkg/lib/Lib__Bar)] is the unit [Lib__Bar] of the library
[lib] in the package [pkg]. [unresolvedroot(Lib__Bar)] is a root that is
not resolved yet. [hidden(...)] marks a path to a hidden unit (S3, section
5). With [--show-expansions] and [--show-include-expansions], [=>] is
followed by the signature odoc computed for a module or an [include].

  $ show() { odoc_print --short --long-paths --show-root-parents --show-expansions --show-include-expansions "$@"; }

odoc recomputes [c]'s [include] from [Lib], so the root [Lib__Bar] in it has
the origin [Lib] (section 3.1). [c] itself has no entry for [Lib__Bar] in
its import table: [Lib] records [Lib__Bar] with no digest, and the compiler
does not copy such a name into the tables of the units that load [Lib].
[entry FILE N], from [../digests.sh], prints [no entry] for it. The root should still be unresolved in
[c]'s file, as its target was not compiled when [Lib] was:

  $ . ../digests.sh
  $ entry c/c.cmti Lib__Bar
  no entry
  $ show h/pkg/c/c.odoc
  include module type of resolved(root(pkg/lib/Lib))
    => sig module Bar/0 = unresolvedroot(Lib__Bar) end

Both [lib] and [libv] are given at link. The root [Lib__Bar] is read back
from [c]'s file, but its origin is still [Lib], which was compiled with
[lib] only. Under D3, [c] can only see the [Lib__Bar] that [Lib] sees, so
this case cannot tell Λc(Lib) from Λc(c). What it can show is that the
root keeps a scope at all: a root that lost its origin would be looked up
among all the libraries given at link, and would find two [Lib__Bar]s. So
[Bar] should mean [lib]'s [Lib__Bar], with no warning. It is hidden, so
odoc should show its expansion inside the [include].

  $ odoc link -L lib:h/pkg/lib -L libv:h/pkg/libv -L c:h/pkg/c h/pkg/c/c.odoc
  $ show h/pkg/c/c.odocl
  include module type of resolved(root(pkg/lib/Lib))
    => sig
      module Bar/0 = resolved(hidden(root(pkg/lib/Lib__Bar)))
        => sig type t/1 end
     end
